  "body": "Stacked on #4201. This PR adds three commits on top of it: `8fd0a47ec..745234df7`.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis is slice 1 of #3645.\n\n- **Project file v84.** A `.camproj` now holds the document tool component table (`components`). Each tool can also hold its component stack (`assembly`).\n  - The loader reads the table and each stack before any world write.\n  - Each link must name a row, and each stack must resolve (the #3643 resolver). If not, the file is refused by the tool name or the component id.\n  - The loader lands the rows and stacks through `table_set` and `set_assembly`. This replaces the clear-on-open line of #4201.\n  - The derived `ToolDef` and `ToolBody` stay as the file states them, so an open does not change a posted program.\n  - An assembled body gets its source and the judged resolver bands back when its drawn outline is the outline that the stack resolves to (`assembly_wire::as_derived`).\n- **One wire form for a component row** (`project::component_wire`), for the project and the library. The codes are written as text: the ISO 1832 insert code, the connection codes, and the ISO 5608 seat letters. The geometry holds the port frames, the body, the cutting point and the bore stops. Each record is read strictly: an unknown key is refused, each row is built again through the checked constructors, and each refusal names the row.\n- **`library_ref { id, content_hash }`** on a document row. The hash is FNV-1a 64 over the wire JSON of the name, the item and the geometry.\n- **User component library** (`component_library`, `component_library::store`):\n  - The file format is `camcraft-components/1` with `units: \"mm\"`.\n  - The folder is `CAMCRAFT_COMPONENTS` (an absolute path). If it is not set, the folder is `<platform data dir>/camcraft/components`. The file is `components.camcomponents`.\n  - A save writes a temp file, then renames it.\n  - The read is all or nothing. The holder library (each entry with a taper) and the starter tool catalog are read-only built-ins in the `builtin:` id space.\n- **Sync.** `sync_status` returns `NotLinked`, `UpToDate`, `UpdateAvailable` or `MissingFromLibrary`. It never applies a library copy.\n  - `SyncDocumentComponent` (undoable) puts the library copy into the row, records the link, and derives each user tool again in one undo step through the `EditDocumentComponent` law (`with_row`).\n  - A hand edit keeps the link.\n  - A change of the link alone derives no tool again.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3645-component-library.md`.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- `PROJECT_VERSION` goes from 83 to 84. Each file that this build writes says v84, so a v83 build refuses it and cannot drop the table. Files of v83 and older open unchanged. This includes #2016 / PR #2092 `holder` references. The commit is `feat(tools)!:` with a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer, as for the v82 and v83 steps and as the issue asks.\n- The `.camtools` format does not change in this PR.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The round trip is byte-stable. The project has six component rows and three assembled tools: two indexable cutters with a shared insert, and one solid end mill in an adapter in a holder (two bodies united band by band).\n- A turned port frame (`x = [0.6, 0.8, 0]`) reads back to the same bits.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nAll the tests are in the existing directory suite `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/`. No new top-level test file.\n\n- `component_files::a_project_with_a_component_table_and_its_assemblies_reopens_identically`\n- `component_files::a_file_without_a_table_and_a_holder_project_open_unchanged`\n- `component_files::a_reader_of_an_older_version_refuses_the_new_file`\n- `component_files::a_corrupt_row_or_link_refuses_the_file_by_name`\n- `component_sync::the_store_round_trips_and_refuses_a_bad_file_whole_by_name`\n- `component_sync::the_save_is_atomic_and_the_env_folder_comes_first`\n- `component_sync::the_built_ins_are_the_holders_and_the_starter_tools_read_only`\n- `component_sync::a_sync_pulls_a_newer_library_copy_into_both_assemblies_and_undo_restores`\n- `component_sync::a_library_copy_that_differs_after_an_open_is_reported_never_applied`\n\n## Gate\n\nAll results are on the final head `745234df789bf856404422bcd1e9202e87be85d2` (Mac).\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 363 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (28.3 min). This includes `tool_library_holders`, `project_roundtrip`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` and the ui suites (`ui suites: machine` too).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed. This ran on head `b376f74fa`. The only later commit is a one-line clippy fix in a test file.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No heavy step: this is a P6 PR.\n- The first quick run was void, because a golden regeneration moved the tree during the run. Its one red step was `continuous_4axis_part`: the committed example project pins `PROJECT_VERSION`. The example now says v84 and changes nothing else. The committed `.nc` program stays as it is.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real platform data folder. The tests use a temp folder and the pure `user_dir_for`.\n- A lathe assembly. `derive` still refuses it (#3643).\n\n## What is left\n\n- On #3645: `.camtools` with components and assemblies. The issue says v5, but `main` is at version 7 (`CUTTER_HAND_VERSION`), so the step is version 8. The import must land the rows through the `ImportTools` undo unit (`commands/tool_import`).\n- #3647: the MCP tools, including `SyncDocumentComponent` and the sync status. No new MCP issue is filed: #3647 covers the component commands.\n- #3648: the UI.\n\nChangelog: Tool components: a project now saves its tool component table and the component stack of each tool (project file v84). A user component library (`components.camcomponents`) holds your own components next to the built-in holders and starter tools. An explicit, undoable sync pulls a library change into a project. Opening a project never applies a library change by itself.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3645\n",
